ComfyUI_PuLID_Flux_ll @ 7c7362b — run on ComfyUI's own Flux forward (ComfyUI >= 0.31)

Why: ApplyPulidFlux's OUTER_SAMPLE wrapper swaps Flux.forward_orig for its own copy
(pulid_forward_orig), written against an older ComfyUI. ComfyUI 0.31 calls forward_orig
with timestep_zero_index, so every sample failed with
  TypeError: pulid_forward_orig() got an unexpected keyword argument 'timestep_zero_index'

Fix: register the node's non-override wrapper instead, so ComfyUI's forward_orig runs
and calls the node's dit block-replace patches itself (it supports them natively). Those
patch classes read transformer_options from extra_options, where only the old forward
put it; ComfyUI passes it in input_args, so they now take whichever is present.
Verified 2026-11-05 on the Halo (ROCm): FLUX.1-dev Q8 GGUF + PuLID v0.9.1, identity kept.

Applied by `stack install comfyui`; `stack doctor` reports whether it is in place.

